.TH "tclinterp::approximation" 3tcl 0\&.15 "tclinterp" "Tcl wrapper for C interpolation procedures"
.SH NAME
tclinterp::approximation - Commands in namespace tclinterp::approximation
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbezier\fP \fI-n integer -a value -b value -x values -y values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBcubicBetaSpline1d\fP \fI-beta1 value -beta2 value -t values -y values -ti values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBcubicBSpline1d\fP \fI-t values -y values -ti values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBgenBezier\fP \fI-n integer -x values -y values -t values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.SH ::TCLINTERP::APPROXIMATION
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBbezier\fR (::tclinterp::approximation)
.RE
.PP
Evaluates a Bezier polynomial on an interval\&.
.RS 4n
\fBbezier\fP \fI-n integer -a value -b value -x values -y values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-a value
Start of the interval; must differ from -b\&.
.TP
-b value
End of the interval; must differ from -a\&.
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-n integer
Polynomial degree; must be zero or greater\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-x values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&.
.TP
-y values
Control values; exactly n+1 values\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The interpolated values yi, as a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output
vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBcubicBetaSpline1d\fR (::tclinterp::approximation)
.RE
.PP
Evaluates a cubic beta-spline approximant\&.
.RS 4n
\fBcubicBetaSpline1d\fP \fI-beta1 value -beta2 value -t values -y values -ti values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-beta1 value
Required skew or bias parameter; 1 means no skew or bias\&.
.TP
-beta2 value
Required tension parameter; 0 means no tension\&.
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-t values
Strictly increasing sample positions; at least two values\&. Alias: -x\&.
.TP
-ti values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&. Alias: -xi\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -t\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
The parameters must produce a finite, nonzero beta-spline normalization\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The approximated values yi, as a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output
vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBcubicBSpline1d\fR (::tclinterp::approximation)
.RE
.PP
Evaluates a cubic B-spline approximant\&.
.RS 4n
\fBcubicBSpline1d\fP \fI-t values -y values -ti values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: yi\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-t values
Strictly increasing sample positions; at least two values\&. Alias: -x\&.
.TP
-ti values
Evaluation positions; must not be empty\&. Alias: -xi\&.
.TP
-y values
Sample values; must have the same length as -t\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
The approximated values yi, as a Tcl list by default or an RBC vector name with -output
vector\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgenBezier\fR (::tclinterp::approximation)
.RE
.PP
Evaluates a parametric Bezier curve\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgenBezier\fP \fI-n integer -x values -y values -t values ?-input list|vector? ?-output list|vector? ?-name name? ?-names dictionary? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists error|replace
Policy for existing destination vectors; defaults to error\&. With replace, an existing real vector is resized and overwritten\&.
.TP
-input list|vector
Input representation for all array arguments: Tcl lists or real RBC vector names\&. Defaults to list\&.
.TP
-n integer
Curve degree; must be zero or greater\&.
.TP
-name name
Destination vector name for yi; requires -output vector\&. Omit it or use #auto to create an automatically named vector\&.
.TP
-names dictionary
Dictionary mapping output fields to destination vector names; requires -output vector\&. Valid fields: xi, yi\&.
.TP
-output list|vector
Output representation for every numeric result array: Tcl list or RBC vector name\&. Defaults to list; independent of -input\&.
.TP
-t values
Nonempty evaluation parameters; normally between 0 and 1\&.
.TP
-x values
X control coordinates; exactly n+1 values\&.
.TP
-y values
Y control coordinates; exactly n+1 values\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Every array argument marked values uses the representation selected by -input\&. Scalar options remain
ordinary Tcl numbers\&. Numeric inputs must be finite\&. RBC support must be enabled in the build to use
vectors\&.
.PP
Vector names resolve in the caller's namespace; destination namespaces must already exist\&. Each unnamed
output, including fields omitted from -names, is created with ::rbc::vector create #auto\&. Returned
vector names are fully qualified\&.
.PP
Do not specify both -name and the yi entry of -names\&. Unknown output fields and duplicate destinations
are errors\&. The caller owns returned vectors and can release them with ::rbc::vector destroy
$vectorName\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
A dictionary with xi and yi coordinates\&. Each numeric array is a Tcl list by default or an
RBC vector name with -output vector\&.


